{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01242",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.18,
      "end_seconds": 7.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting, come in. So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.75,
      "end_seconds": 13.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "um, so... numbness in my feet that's why I came"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.36,
      "end_seconds": 18.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.0,
      "end_seconds": 29.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "nearly done with the readings.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.53,
      "end_seconds": 54.73,
      "duration_seconds": 11.2,
      "text": "okay: oxygen saturation is 96 percent, temp 38.4 degrees, pulse is 108 beats a minute, respiratory rate 22, BP is 104 over 71."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.68,
      "end_seconds": 58.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Is that alright, you know, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.92,
      "end_seconds": 65.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "we'll go over that shortly how many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.42,
      "end_seconds": 68.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "I've had it since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.24,
      "end_seconds": 73.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.4,
      "end_seconds": 87.78,
      "duration_seconds": 12.38,
      "text": "mostly moderate i've had redness around the sore too, for ten days i did have a smell from the dressing at one point, but that's gone now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.23,
      "end_seconds": 94.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "Any pain at rest in the leg, vomiting, confusion or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.5,
      "end_seconds": 97.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.6,
      "end_seconds": 106.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.18,
      "end_seconds": 111.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "no, that side's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.86,
      "end_seconds": 117.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "So, what conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.4,
      "end_seconds": 121.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "I have diabetes. I have high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.26,
      "end_seconds": 126.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Alright, diabetes, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.82,
      "end_seconds": 138.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "okay, have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.96,
      "end_seconds": 143.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Yes, I had an operation for a hernia, last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.27,
      "end_seconds": 164.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Alright, who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.22,
      "end_seconds": 170.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.32,
      "end_seconds": 174.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.31,
      "end_seconds": 179.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.63,
      "end_seconds": 197.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.94,
      "end_seconds": 203.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "I'm on sitagliptin, once a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.67,
      "end_seconds": 206.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.33,
      "end_seconds": 216.74,
      "duration_seconds": 8.41,
      "text": "100 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box. It's rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.49,
      "end_seconds": 220.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "How long has that been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.92,
      "end_seconds": 228.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "For about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.21,
      "end_seconds": 230.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.33,
      "end_seconds": 235.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "I used to take simvastatin, but I stopped it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.39,
      "end_seconds": 242.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.27,
      "end_seconds": 246.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "tell me if that's sore"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.94,
      "end_seconds": 265.3,
      "duration_seconds": 7.36,
      "text": "There is a two-centimetre ulcer on the ball of the right foot with redness around it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.59,
      "end_seconds": 305.99,
      "duration_seconds": 36.4,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. From what you've told me and what I found, I'm honestly not certain yet. It could be an infected diabetic foot ulcer, or it might be pressure damage. A swab from the ulcer is what I'd like next, for infected ulcer. The treatment will be amoxicillin/clavulanic acid, 625 milligrams, three times a day, for seven days. That's for foot infection. Keep the weight off that foot and keep the dressing dry."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.35,
      "end_seconds": 312.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "let's get you seen by the foot clinic, I'll arrange the letter"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 313.8,
      "end_seconds": 316.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.49,
      "end_seconds": 328.94,
      "duration_seconds": 11.45,
      "text": "I'd like to to see you again after the swab result. Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.06,
      "end_seconds": 342.04,
      "duration_seconds": 11.98,
      "text": "So, I take the amoxicillin/clavulanic acid, 625 milligrams, three times a day and come back after the swab result. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.09,
      "end_seconds": 349.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. So, I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.98,
      "end_seconds": 353.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    }
  ]
}